<title>UK: TABLE - Liberty Plc returns to profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Liberty Plc returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to February 1.</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		17.51 (profit)    vs 79.63 (loss)</p>
<p> Shr ex-excepts (pence)  9.23		 vs  3.58</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  1.85		 vs  nil</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  1.85		 vs  1.85</p>
<p> Pretax profit	     4.4		  vs 16.6 (loss)</p>
<p> Turnover		   80.9		  vs 85.7</p>
<p>Note - The retailer said there had been an exceptional profit of 0.8 million stg relating to major restructuring of operations. Last year there had been an exceptional charge of 18.7 million stg charge for restructuring. The company said trading in the current year has been satisfactory and in line with expectations.</p>
<p>Full company name - Liberty Plc</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
